# Extra exemptions for lint_numerals.py — one regex per line.
#
# Only add patterns for things that are NAMES or CONVENTIONS, never for
# measurements. If a number could differ between two runs of the seeded model,
# it does not belong here — it belongs in a helper.
#
# Calibrate on first run: expect false positives from domain vocabulary, and
# expect a few true findings you will want to fix rather than exempt.

# --- coded factor levels: conventions of the coding scheme -----------------
[−\-+±]?[01](?:\s*/\s*[−\-+±]?[01])+
±\s*1\b
\bset-point is 0\b
\bcoded (?:levels?|settings?|units?)[^.]*\b

# --- appendix and design labels -------------------------------------------
\bAppendix\s+[A-Z]\d?\b
\bfactors?\s+[A-Z]–[A-Z]\b
\bResolution\s+[IV]+\b

# --- markdown ordered-list markers ----------------------------------------
^\s*\d+\.\s

# --- process and assay nomenclature (added for PCR-008/009/010, PTP, RA) ---
\b[Rr]uns?\s+\d+\b
[Ww]ash-\d\b
\bEquil/Wash-\d\b
\bSteps?\s+\d+(?:\s*[–-]\s*\d+)?\b
\bN-\d\b
\bTCID\d+\b
log(?:₁₀|10)\b
\bQ\d[A-Z]?\(R\d\)\b
\b\d{3}\s*nm\b
\bqPCR\b
\bMVM\b
\bXMuLV\b
\b[A-Z]-Mab\b

# --- NOT exempted, deliberately -------------------------------------------
# alpha = 0.05, p > 0.05, p < 0.001  -> results and study-design decisions;
#                                       make them helpers so text and annex
#                                       cannot disagree
# n = 4 replicates                   -> a real count from the design
# 95% confidence/prediction interval -> a study-design decision
# effect = 2 x coded coefficient     -> definitional, but worth a helper
# 15/25 degC in PCR-006 fig caption  -> a hardcoded measurement
